<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The colour Android paints before Flutter is running.

    The slate-900 token from the PWA's tokens.css, light side: the furthest
    surface from the reader. On paper that means the palest, which is why this
    file and the values-night one look inverted rather than merely different.

    (Token names are written without their leading dashes on purpose — XML
    forbids a double hyphen inside a comment and the build fails on it.)

    ── The case this cannot get right ──────────────────────────────────────
    The app's theme is a preference, not the system setting, so somebody who
    runs their phone light and chose dark in Settings still gets a pale launch
    window for a frame. Fixing that would mean writing the choice somewhere
    Android can read before Dart starts, which is a second copy of a setting —
    and a second copy is a thing that can disagree. Following the system is
    right for everyone who has not overridden it, which is nearly everyone.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="launch_background">#f4f2ed</color>
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#0d0f12</color>
</resources>
